From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0710: HDR at SDR cost on the 880M: the HDR scene computed inside the swap's refresher (hdr_scene_fused), UI by difference, refresher source straight from the front buffer's render target, trims of the UI-layer path (hdr_trim, hdr_ui_mode)

Source: Ours, written for this SDK (stream HDR) on top of Renan Queiroz's rexglue-hdr-output / -hdr-ui-layer /
  -hdr-scene-mcla (GPL-3, unchanged in the series; this patch changes their code paths) and our 04a0 (swap_direct_present).
  The scene math is Renan's hdr_scene_mcla.cs.xesl moved into hdr_scene_mcla.xesli unchanged (its DXBC is byte-identical).
  DXBC built with fxc 10.0.26100 (Renan's recipe, D3D12 only; Vulkan SPIR-V untouched: Vulkan keeps the old paths).
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched files are ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause)
Purpose: Renan's HDR (UI separated into a layer + an RGBA16F HDR scene image + a copy of the tone map output, all composed
  in the swap's refresher) costs ~1.8 ms GPU per frame at 1080p on the Radeon 880M (bandwidth-bound; run hdr2: GPU busy
  median 16.71 ms vs 14.93 SDR). This patch makes it ~0.1-0.3 ms (run hdr3: fused 13.41 ms vs SDR 13.13 median, +0.10 mean):
  * hdr_scene_fused (bool, default true; D3D12): at the tone map draw nothing is drawn: its four inputs (FP16 scene, blur,
    bloom, adapted luminance) and constants are captured (resource refs + SRV descs; a texture-cache content serial,
    bumped by every load and dual-write resolve, proves at the swap that none was rewritten, else that frame keeps the
    8-bit scene, logged). The refresher (new variant hdr_refresh_fused.cs) computes the HDR scene per pixel inline with the
    same math and also the game's own 8-bit tone map result, which stands in for the tone map copy in the glow test.
    The UI goes by difference against one pre-UI snapshot (composite 1). No FP16 scene image, no tone-map copy, no
    UI-layer clear/copy/restore.
  * hdr_scene_fused_check (int N, default 0): every Nth fused frame the old passes run too and a compute counts the
    differences (readback, no stall): run hdr3, 84 checks: 0 scene mismatches (max rel 0), 0 tone map pixels off by more
    than one code (8.7 % one code off, inside the glow test's 1.5/255 tolerance).
  * The HDR refresher reads the front buffer from its host render target through 04a0's record instead of loading the
    swap texture (counted in 04a0's 10 s line as "made from the render target").
  * hdr_trim (bool, default true; D3D12): for the UI-layer path (hdr_scene_fused=false or Vulkan): skip the swap texture
    load when the refresher does not read it, skip the UI-layer clear when one copy covers the output, alias the underlay
    to its snapshot when the copy is a whole-output identity (run hdr2: -0.44 ms).
  * hdr_ui_mode (layer | diff, default layer): the UI by difference without the fused scene.
  Logs once per change: "HDR: scene fused into the refresher (...)", "HDR: trim (...)", "HDR: fused check #k: ...".
  Off (hdr off): no new work. Also: the textures this path doesn't use are never created.
Bucket: REDO

Edits outside the HDR code (additive): TextureCache::Texture content serial + FindTexture
(pipeline/texture/cache.h/.cpp), D3D12TextureCache::CaptureActiveTexture / UseCapturedTexture (d3d12/texture_cache.*).
---
